{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/858765-the-state-of-vampire","id":858765,"title":"The State of Vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-03T21:43:34-07:00","id":858765,"title":"The State of Vampire","content":"So we've gone with some radio silence for awhile now with regards to Vampire. I saw on the Monday Meeting notes that Mike Chaney says the last bit of art is on its way for Secrets of the Covenant, so that's good, but there just don't appear to be any books at any other stages at all. With the other gamelines we have a sense of the books coming out, though we don't know when, and we hear stuff generally from Stew and Dave about what's going on with Werewolf and Mage, but we're getting nothing on Vampire's front.<br /> <br /> Please, throw us a bone! Something! Anything! What's going on with Vampire, and is there anything going on besides <i>Secrets of the Covenants</i>? What are the plans for the other books? Is there any kind of vision? I remember hearing that there would be more blogposts with content for Vampire, and that some of the writers were even sitting on ideas, but once again, heard nothing about the game.<br /> <br /> Vampire is my favorite line, but the lack of communication of anything can be a real bummer. It almost seems like Vampire got mucked up worse than any other lines as a consequence of this Paradox uncertainty.<br /> <br /> What's going on, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a>? Even just a little teaser or thought would be like water in the desert.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T21:47:58-07:00","id":858767,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'm curious too. There's a bunch of stuff that I know they were going to put in blogs; several bloodlines, ritual conversions from 1e, as well as potentially details for the elder and half-splat books, but none of it ever came. It's gotten to the point of being disconcerting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T22:31:45-07:00","id":858781,"title":"","content":"Isn't there a book about Elders on the way called Thousand Years Of Night?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T22:35:29-07:00","id":858783,"title":"","content":"At least we got Requiem for Regina and we'll be getting that Black Death setting in the Dark Eras Companion, but yeah. Very curious about more Vampire.<br /> <br /> Previews for Thousand Years of Night would be fantastic, even just the outline for it (like we saw with the Demon Storyteller's Guide).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 04-04-2016, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T23:09:25-07:00","id":858787,"title":"","content":"Right now,Vampire is in Wisconsin.<br /> <br /> Someone took a wrong turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":