t</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would have to be one hell of a wrong turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering Bugs Bunny one ended up in a bullfight in Spain after such a turn, that's not so surprising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T18:48:29-07:00","id":859377,"title":"","content":"I was looking over the release catalogue for Vampire and realized we basically haven't gotten any new books since 2013, and that's very depressing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I guess it should be said that, given Vampire was the forerunner of the 2nd Editions, it shouldn't be surprising that it has &quot;suffered&quot; the most with the changing of formats, changing of IP holders and so on. I'm just bummed out, because I really love Vampire and want more books to show how good it can be.<br /> <br /> Oh, and that content for <i>Dark Eras</i>. I'm a huge fan of <i>Requiem for Regina</i>. Maybe I'm being unkind here, I just got a lot of love and feel kinda burned by the silence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 04-04-2016, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T19:24:52-07:00","id":859393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/858765-the-state-of-vampire?p=859377#post859377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was looking over the release catalogue for Vampire and realized we basically haven't gotten any new books since 2013, and that's very depressing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I guess it should be said that, given Vampire was the forerunner of the 2nd Editions, it shouldn't be surprising that it has &amp;quot;suffered&amp;quot; the most with the changing of formats, changing of IP holders and so on. I'm just bummed out, because I really love Vampire and want more books to show how good it can be.<br /> <br /> Oh, and that content for <i>Dark Eras</i>. I'm a huge fan of <i>Requiem for Regina</i>. Maybe I'm being unkind here, I just got a lot of love and feel kinda burned by the silence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely getcha. Werewolf is still relatively new and Mage isn't even out yet, but we're getting /tons/ of interaction with developers and freelancers and all sorts of exciting previews and what.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Vampire has basically gone quiet beyond originally announcing a handful of books and those early Open Development blogs for the mechanics in Secrets of the Covenants. It's not just that Vampire has had so little, it's that all the games around it have been pretty bursting with stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T23:51:13-07:00","id":860149,"title":"","content":"Still thinking about this, and still generally sad about the radio silence. Saw in the Monday Meeting Notes that we're still waiting on more art to get in to Secrets of the Covenants. Definitely makes sense, it's an art heavy book like the Clanbooks.<br /> <br /> Could we get a teaser or a discussion of what's coming next?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:41:32-07:00","id":860600,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry. I've got two lines in my care, as well as overseeing the CofD as a whole (which means going through a revision process on every book, as well as developing some, and work on all the second editions) and being in charge of development/editing production for Onyx Path as a company. Plus more stuff I can't mention, and doing everything with only one usable arm.<br /> <br /> So I'm slowed down. To address that, I'm bringing in a co-developer on Vampire, starting with A Thousand Years of Night.<br /> <br /> Here's what's coming:<ul><li><b>Secrets of the Covenants: </b>Mike needs some time on it, but the manuscript's been locked down and approved by Paradox for a while now.</li> <li><b>A Thousand Years of Night: </b>Paradox just approved the outline, which goes to writers over the weekend. I or my co-developer, Danielle Lauzon, will post the outline.</li> <li><b>Half-Damned: </b>Working on mechanics for this; once that framework's together, it'll go to outline, approval, etc.</li> <li><b>Guide to the Night: </b>The last currently announced title, this one's large and ambitious -- it's supposed to be a top-to-bottom guide to running and playing the game. You'll see a few familiar concepts, like how to use Tiers to scope your setting, but it's mostly new territory. We'll be covering how to create characters and link them to the world, how to run games for more (and less) self-directed groups, and a lot more. EDIT: Also probably a whole bunch of Climbing the Ladder type stuff.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 04-06-2016, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":25}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"r