https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T15:57:18-07:00","id":862238,"title":"","content":"One of my favorite Open Development blogs of all time was when the raw outline for the Demon Storyteller's Guide got shared. Is there any hope of us seeing something like that for an upcoming Requiem supplement? It's a great way to generate excitement and it's stuff that already exists in a Word document somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T17:57:22-07:00","id":862313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/858765-the-state-of-vampire?p=860600#post860600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry. I've got two lines in my care, as well as overseeing the CofD as a whole (which means going through a revision process on every book, as well as developing some, and work on all the second editions) and being in charge of development/editing production for Onyx Path as a company. Plus more stuff I can't mention, and doing everything with only one usable arm.<br /> <br /> So I'm slowed down. To address that, I'm bringing in a co-developer on Vampire, starting with A Thousand Years of Night.<br /> <br /> Here's what's coming:<ul><li><b>Secrets of the Covenants: </b>Mike needs some time on it, but the manuscript's been locked down and approved by Paradox for a while now.</li> <li><b>A Thousand Years of Night: </b>Paradox just approved the outline, which goes to writers over the weekend. I or my co-developer, Danielle Lauzon, will post the outline.</li> <li><b>Half-Damned: </b>Working on mechanics for this; once that framework's together, it'll go to outline, approval, etc.</li> <li><b>Guide to the Night: </b>The last currently announced title, this one's large and ambitious -- it's supposed to be a top-to-bottom guide to running and playing the game. You'll see a few familiar concepts, like how to use Tiers to scope your setting, but it's mostly new territory. We'll be covering how to create characters and link them to the world, how to run games for more (and less) self-directed groups, and a lot more. EDIT: Also probably a whole bunch of Climbing the Ladder type stuff.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Not to sound greedy, but I'm totally am being greedy. Any chance of you spoiling something for Secret of the Covenant? You know to let us see the difference made so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}